`benchmark.meta description: Processes a long synthetic Markdown document.
`benchmark.meta timing: recommended
`benchmark.meta profiles: compile-timing

/data/markdown

. source = long-markdown-document()
. checksum = 0 as Size
for i in 0 .. < 18
    . rendered = markdown-to-html(Markdown(source))
    checksum += rendered.length * (i + 1)
    checksum += source.length

-- "bench-result markdown/long-document checksum=$checksum"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ long-markdown-document

"# Deterministic Transcript\n\n" ++ (markdown-section() * 80)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ¶ markdown-section

## Assistant Message

This synthetic transcript paragraph mixes **strong text**, *emphasis*, `inline code`, and [a stable link](https://example.com/static/path). It mentions identifiers_like_this, numeric values 12345 and 67890, and a short sentence that wraps in rich text layouts.

* First bullet with [reference](https://example.com/ref)
    * Nested detail with `code`
    * Another nested detail with **bold**
* Second bullet with *italic* text

> A stable blockquote keeps quoted rendering pressure in the document.

```
let answer = 42
print(answer)
```
